% expect-output: before
% expect-output: after
% expect-output: 1
% Scenario: currentfile closefile inside an eexec section given a string.
% PLRM3 §8.2: eexec makes a file object over the file OR the string and
% that file is the current one, so the section's own `currentfile
% closefile` ends the section and the outer source continues — the
% "encrypted text followed by unencrypted text" shape the manual
% describes. A driver's prologue ends its downloads that way. Treating a
% string section as a bare string source instead hid it from
% `currentfile`, which found the job's file and closed that, ending the
% whole job silently.
% The section below decrypts to: userdict /inside 1 put currentfile closefile
% Expect: before, after, 1.
(before) =
<81B87280B0B710FE7B75F2BFFD138BF3116C2C9060B55C6E8DD24E0B4C0486901487403641009A323E40A70398D5C2E7> eexec
(after) =
inside =
